Get it yourself:
  1. Download the UNSPSC English workbook from https://www.unspsc.org
     (you may need to register and accept UNDP's terms).
  2. Save it as data/unspsc_english.xlsx.
  3. Build the local search list:  node scripts/build-subset.js
     This writes data/unspsc-subset.csv. Both files are gitignored.
     (Needs the `unzip` binary; no npm dependencies.)

Without the list, LineGrade still runs: it replays a saved, labelled run of a
SYNTHETIC catalog. Live AI re-runs and the full code search need the list and
are disabled. The saved catalog (data/enriched-catalog.json) records, for the
codes the AI chose, the code and the title the classifier returned for it.
Those titles are UNDP's and remain subject to UNDP's terms.
